row(33, 38, 'MATERIAL', f'AND AARON THE PRIEST WENT UP MOUNT HOR BY THE MOUTH OF THE LORD AND DIED THERE, IN THE FORTIETH YEAR OF THE GOING OUT OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL FROM THE LAND OF EGYPT, IN THE FIFTH MONTH, ON THE FIRST OF THE MONTH — THE TORAH\'S ONE FULL DEATH-DATE, THE TAPE\'S OWN MARKER. {HP(33, 38, (("ויעל", "אהרן", "הכהן", "אל", "הר", "ההר"), "and Aaron the priest went up Mount Hor — 20:25-27\'s ascent (\'take Aaron and Eleazar his son and bring them up Mount Hor\')"), (("על", "פי", "יהוה", "וימת", "שם"), "BY THE MOUTH OF THE LORD and died there — the phrase\'s second seat in the chapter (33:2 Moses wrote by it); 20:28 narrates the death with no date (computed)"), (("בשנת", "הארבעים"), "IN THE FORTIETH YEAR — the article form\'s two Bible seats (this; 1 Chronicles 26:31, David\'s fortieth); the parser reads the year as an ORDINAL [40] by the article-bearing numeral (rule 20, the Torah\'s one seat of the form); Deuteronomy 1:3\'s \'in the fortieth year, in the eleventh month, on the first of the month\' is written in cardinal forms and the number reader gives [40, 11, 1] (computed)"), (("לצאת", "בני", "ישראל", "מארץ", "מצרים"), "of the going out of the children of Israel from the land of Egypt — three Bible seats: Exodus 19:1 (the third month, Sinai), this (the fortieth year, Mount Hor), 1 Kings 6:1 (the four hundred and eightieth year, the temple\'s founding) — THE ERA\'S THREE STAMPS in that form (computed)"), (("בחדש", "החמישי", "באחד", "לחדש"), "IN THE FIFTH MONTH, ON THE FIRST OF THE MONTH — the fifth month the Torah\'s one seat (Jeremiah 1:3, 28:1, Ezra 7:8 the others); \'on the first of the month\' ten Torah seats; the parser: ordinals [40, 5] and the number [1] = (40, 5, 1) — THE TAPE\'S MARKER FOR AARON\'S DEATH AT 20:28 IS BUILT FROM THIS VERSE (cold_run_sequence.py reads 33:38\'s ordinals and number into day_in; CM2 checks (40, 5, 1)): the reading\'s measurement equals the tape\'s marker (computed)"))} → {AP(33, 38, (("וסלק", "אהרן", "כהנא", "להור", "טורא"), "and Aaron the priest went up to Hor the mountain"), (("על", "מימרא", "דיי", "ומית", "תמן"), "by THE WORD of the LORD and died there — the buffer\'s second seat"), (("בשנת", "ארבעין", "למפק", "בני", "ישראל"), "in the year forty of the going out of the children of Israel — the cardinal in the Aramaic where the Hebrew has the article-bearing ordinal"), (("מארעא", "דמצרים", "בירחא", "חמשאה", "בחד", "לירחא"), "from the land of Egypt, in the fifth month, on the first of the month"))}.')
